{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeightWenzl","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeightWenzl","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Nat","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeight","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.WenzlWeightVanishing"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightWenzl.lean#L151-L167","doc":"**The two-row cap for the derived weight, as an `iff`.**\n\n`ocneanuWeight q (q³/(q²+1)) μ = 0 ↔ μ has more than two rows.`\n\nNot proved here: it is `QBeta.WenzlWeight.schurPrincipal_eq_zero_iff` transported along the bridge.\n`OcneanuWeight.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_zero_of_three_rows` proves the forward direction\ndirectly and needs no root-of-unity hypothesis; this is the sharper statement and needs `hgen`,\nexactly as the corpus theorem does — at a root of unity a hook length can kill a denominator and the\n`iff` is false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_schurPrincipal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_schurPrincipal","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightWenzl.lean#L121-L149","doc":"**The bridge.**  The derived general-`n` Ocneanu weight, evaluated at convention D's Markov\nparameter, is the level-2 principal Schur specialisation up to the normalisation `[2]_{q²}^{|μ|}`:\n\n`ocneanuWeight q (q³/(q²+1)) μ = schurPrincipal 2 (q²) μ / (q²+1)^{|μ|}`\n\nfor every Young diagram — no genericity hypothesis on `q` beyond `q ≠ 0` and `q² + 1 ≠ 0`.\n\nSee the module docstring for what this settles (the two objects are the same) and what it does not\n(the Markov property of either at general `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.schurPrincipalNumFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.schurPrincipalNumFactor","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightWenzl.lean#L109-L119","doc":"The `schurPrincipal` numerator factor of the cell `(i,j)`, with the `Q^{n(λ)}` prefactor\ndistributed one power per cell: `Q^i · (1 − Q^{2 + c}) = q^{2i} − q^{2j+4}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuNumFactor_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightWenzl.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**The per-cell identity.**  At `z = q³/(q²+1)` the numerator factor of the cell `(i,j)`\ncollapses to `(q^{2j+4} − q^{2i})/(q²+1)` — a difference of two monomials over the fixed\ndenominator `q²+1`.  This is the whole content of the bridge; everything else is bookkeeping. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.hookLength_eq_hook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.hookLength_eq_hook","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/OcneanuWeightWenzl.lean#L60-L95","doc":"`OcneanuWeight.hookLength` (a `Finset.card`, hence `decide`-evaluable on concrete diagrams)\nagrees on cells with `QOU.QBeta.WenzlWeight.hook` (arm + leg via `rowLen`/`colLen`).\n\nTwo definitions of one notion is a duplication; this lemma is the price of the computable one, and\nis stated so that no other file has to choose between them. ","signatureChunk":0}]}